infographic hierarchy-mindmap-level-gradient-compact-card
data
  title The modern hint vocabulary (Python 3.10+)
  desc Five tools that turn anonymous dicts and stringly-typed flags into contracts a checker can enforce — at zero runtime cost
  root
    label A checkable contract
    children
      - label X | Y unions
        desc PEP 604 — replaces Optional/Union. One bar admits None, so -> User | None can no longer hide a missing row.
      - label Generic built-ins
        desc list[int], dict[str, Decimal] parametrize directly — no typing.List imports for everyday collections.
      - label TypedDict
        desc Names and checks an anonymous dict's keys and value types; stays a plain dict at runtime, so no caller breaks.
      - label Literal
        desc Closes a stringly-typed flag set to a fixed list — a typo'd mode is a build failure, not a 3 a.m. KeyError.
      - label Annotated
        desc Carries metadata (units, validation) that pydantic and FastAPI read, while checkers see only the underlying type.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #8b5cf6
